ROLE: theory_skeptic  VOTE: green
MUNDANE_EXPLANATIONS: [RoPE bakes absolute position into K, so identical token spans at different offsets yield non-identical K tensors — this is textbook RoPE algebra (Su et al. 2021, RoFormer §3.4.2), not an emergent finding; the 0.35–1.46% position-aware residual is exactly the expected coincidence rate of two random offsets matching mod sequence length given small N and short shared spans; the noshift control's 59% abspos_frac is trivially predicted because aligned schemas land at the same offset by construction.]
CONFOUNDS: [word-level tokenizer (1 word ≈ 1 token) inflates chunk-boundary stability vs. real BPE — real tokenizer would likely DECREASE token-level dup (subword splits at tenant-filler boundaries), strengthening the negative, not weakening it; block_size=16 is arbitrary — but sensitivity is bounded since position-aware requires exact abs-pos match regardless of block size; N≤128 tenants is small, but the abspos_frac trend (0.0→7.1%) is going the WRONG way for the claim (still ≪10% threshold).]
ASSUMPTIONS_UNTESTED: [no actual K-tensor cosine/MSE measured — paper assumes raw-KV equality is the bar, but an approximate-dedup tolerance band (cosine > 0.99) was not measured and could in principle rescue some shifted spans; the "intra-block phase" relaxation (offset ≡ mod block_size) was pre-registered as a sensitivity but no number is reported in the headline table; cost of R(Δ) re-rotation transform is asserted "cheap" but not measured vs. recompute FLOPs.]
STATISTICAL_GAPS: [single seed (20260603) — no variance across seeds reported, so the 0.35–1.46% range conflates N-effect with seed noise; no confidence intervals on abspos_frac; no power analysis — but for a NEGATIVE verdict against a ">10%" threshold with observed effect ~1%, the gap is ~10σ even under generous variance assumptions, so statistical insufficiency does not threaten the negative direction; the noshift control is n=1 config, fine as a sanity check but not a distribution.]
RATIONALE: The negative verdict is correctly grounded in first-principles RoPE position-dependence — this is not a surprising finding, it is the textbook prediction (RoFormer, Su et al. 2021), and the experiment honestly measured both the optimistic (token-level 4–7%) and honest (position-aware 0.35–1.46%) numbers per pre-registration. The decision rule was committed pre-run (8c4c339 lineage stated) and the negative branch fires cleanly on condition (a). The noshift control correctly demonstrates the mechanism exists but is captured by exact-prefix in exactly the regime where it works, which is the right falsifier. Mundane-explanation check: yes, the result IS predicted by basic theory (that's a feature for a NEGATIVE), and the researcher names the only revival path (CacheBlend-style R(Δ) re-rotation, cited as known prior art) without overclaiming. Statistical gaps (single seed, no CIs) are real but harmless given the ~10× gap to threshold. The prior-art owed (LMCache/CacheBlend/KVQuant) is explicitly flagged as a sweep owed before any HELD/PARTIAL — appropriate scoping for a NEGATIVE L0.
